@cindex Jacobi elliptic functions
@cindex elliptic functions (Jacobi)

The Jacobian Elliptic functions are defined in Abramowitz & Stegun,
Chapter 16.  The functions are declared in the header file
@file{gsl_sf_elljac.h}.

@deftypefun int gsl_sf_elljac_e (double @var{u}, double @var{m}, double * @var{sn}, double * @var{cn}, double * @var{dn})
This function computes the Jacobian elliptic functions @math{sn(u|m)},
@math{cn(u|m)}, @math{dn(u|m)} by descending Landen
transformations.
@comment Exceptional Return Values: GSL_EDOM
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun int gsl_sf_elljac_arcsn_e (double @var{sn}, double @var{m}, gsl_sf_result * @var{result})
@deftypefunx int gsl_sf_elljac_arccn_e (double @var{cn}, double @var{m}, gsl_sf_result * @var{result})
@deftypefunx int gsl_sf_elljac_arcdn_e (double @var{dn}, double @var{m}, gsl_sf_result * @var{result})
These functions compute the principal value @math{u} of the inverse
Jacobian elliptic functions with the parameter @var{m}
(@math{|m| \le 1}), so that @math{sn(u|m) = sn}, @math{cn(u|m) = cn}
and @math{dn(u|m) = dn} respectively.  The principal value satisfies
@math{0 \le u \le 2K(m)}.  The parameter @var{m} is used rather than the
modulus @math{k = \sqrt{m}}, matching @code{gsl_sf_elljac_e}; negative
values of @var{m} are supported.  The inverse of @math{dn} is not
defined for @math{m = 0}, where @math{dn(u|0) = 1} for every @math{u}.
@comment Exceptional Return Values: GSL_EDOM
@end deftypefun

@deftypefun double gsl_sf_elljac_arcsn (double @var{sn}, double @var{m})
@deftypefunx double gsl_sf_elljac_arccn (double @var{cn}, double @var{m})
@deftypefunx double gsl_sf_elljac_arcdn (double @var{dn}, double @var{m})
These functions return the same values as the corresponding
@code{_e} functions, using the default error handler.
@end deftypefun
